%erg 0.1
Title: Housekeeping should delete stale branches for closed tickets
Created: 2026-05-11
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-05-11T21:30Z MinhHaDuong created
2026-05-12T21:00Z claude note — reimagine: case 2 (empty orphan branches) deferred as stretch goal. Core fix: reclassify closed-ticket branches with 0 commits_beyond_default from cleanup-candidate to fix-now in healthcheck SKILL.md. Use git branch -d (not -D) — fails safely on unmerged. Open-PR guard via gh pr list --head.

--- body ---
## Context

Healthcheck check 4 (Branch hygiene) flags local branches whose ticket is
closed as "cleanup candidates." But housekeeping never acts on this — no
fix-now item deletes stale branches. The result: branches accumulate and
`erg ready` misreports tickets as claimed because it uses branch-name
substring matching.

Observed tonight in chemin-de-voix: 4 tickets (0013, 0015, 0070, 0079)
showed as claimed despite stale claims, because empty branches existed.
6 more branches for closed tickets (0119–0122) and orphaned worktree
branches also lingered.

## Design

Add branch cleanup to the housekeeping fix-now pipeline. Two cases:

1. **Closed-ticket branches** — branch name contains a 4-digit ticket ID,
   that ticket has a `Closed:` header or lives under `closed/`, and the
   branch has no unmerged commits (all commits reachable from default
   branch, possibly via squash-merge). Delete with `git branch -d` or
   `git branch -D` after verifying commits are landed.

2. **Empty orphan branches** — branches with 0 commits beyond the default
   branch, no associated worktree, and no open PR. Delete with
   `git branch -d`.

Worktree-locked branches (`+` prefix in `git branch`) must have their
worktree removed first (`git worktree remove`). Only remove worktrees
with no uncommitted changes; skip dirty ones and flag them as warn.

Healthcheck already collects `branches.details` with `commits_beyond_default`
and worktree association. The probe data is sufficient — no new git commands
needed.

## Actions

1. In healthcheck SKILL.md check 4, classify deletable branches as fix-now
   (not just "cleanup candidates").
2. In housekeeping step 3, add branch deletion: remove orphaned worktrees
   first, then delete branches. Log each deletion.
3. Guard: never delete a branch that has an open PR (`gh pr list --head`).

## Exit criteria

1. Housekeeping deletes local branches for closed tickets when commits are
   already on the default branch.
2. Housekeeping removes orphaned worktrees (clean only) before deleting
   their branches.
3. Branches with open PRs or dirty worktrees are skipped with a warning.
4. chemin-de-voix `erg ready` no longer shows false claimed tickets after
   a housekeeping run.
